From 4025259e1f7c7874c2c8f0a0178d59d83b4780f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:42:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rotations and evaluations of material properties on views

- rotateGradients, rotateThermodynamicForces and
  rotateTangentOperatorBlocks take views with arbitrary strides: rotation
  matrices given by a view or built from material axes, in place or not,
  without policy, with a synchronous or an asynchronous policy.
- evaluate takes views for the output and the inputs, with the three
  execution forms.
- one code path: the overloads taking arrays build views and call the
  same functions. The behaviours of the generic interface rotate point by
  point, through a buffer of one point if the components are not
  contiguous.
- evaluate no longer allocates the arrays of the arguments and of the
  strides on the heap at each call.
- tests: rotations and evaluations on views compared bit by bit to the
  overloads taking arrays, for all the layouts, and on the device with
  CUDA.
